Package: rplatypus
Type: Package
Title: Computer Vision for Medical Imaging
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Michal", "Maj", email = "michalmaj116@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Semantic segmentation and object detection for medical images, from a
    folder of pictures to a trained model and a figure, in a handful of lines or one
    configuration file. Architectures, losses and training run on 'PyTorch' through
    'pyplatypus', a 'Python' package which is installed and isolated automatically;
    nothing has to be set up by hand. R keeps the parts that make an analysis fast -
    reading and combining masks, drawing boxes, plotting, comparing models.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/maju116/rplatypus, https://maju116.github.io/rplatypus/
BugReports: https://github.com/maju116/rplatypus/issues
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10). Not a prerequisite the user installs:
    the package declares what it needs through 'reticulate' and 'uv' provisions an
    isolated environment on first use, leaving any system Python untouched.
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    ggplot2,
    grDevices,
    parallel,
    rlang,
    reticulate (>= 1.41),
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
